# The shared libraries' suite. Every variable it reads is one `env` prints already (DBDATAKIT_TEST_MSSQL_SERVER / _USER / _PASSWORD / _ODBC,
# DBDATAKIT_TEST_POSTGRES); what is added here is the name of the State suites, DBDATAKIT_TEST_SQLSERVER, which the `dbdatakit-older` map points at
# SQL Server 2022 instead, so the two maps never print it with different values in one shell.
DBDATAKIT_TEST_SQLSERVER           <- DBDATAKIT_TEST_MSSQL
# Engines the job started are required: a server that does not answer fails the run instead of skipping its tests.
DBDATAKIT_TEST_REQUIRE_SQLSERVER = true if DBDATAKIT_TEST_MSSQL
